<section id="s1">
<h2>1. Product Overview</h2>
<p>A mobile-first, browser-based, multiplayer party game. One <strong>Host</strong> runs a live session of a scripted role-play story for up to 6 <strong>Players</strong>, all in the same room, each on their own phone. The Host picks a fixed script (horror, adventure, etc.), assigns each player a character, and starts the game. Each player sees only their own line, only on their turn, then swipes to advance. Embedded sound cues play on specific devices or across the whole room, creating a shared audio-narrative experience, similar in spirit to Kahoot! but for atmospheric group storytelling.</p>
<p>The Host chooses one of two modes in the lobby. <strong>Story Mode</strong> is the immersive original. <strong>Challenge Mode</strong> adds Secret Objectives and Reaction Races, scored across the session with a final leaderboard. Both modes use the same script; challenge content is flagged <code>challenge_only</code> and skipped in Story Mode.</p>
<p>No accounts are required. Sessions are ephemeral and identified by a short room code.</p>
</section>

<section id="s2">
<h2>2. Core User Roles</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Role</th><th>Description</th></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Host</strong></td><td>Creates the session, picks the script and mode, assigns characters, starts/pauses the game, and advances auto-read and surprise-intruder lines. Sees unassigned characters' lines. In Challenge Mode, sees the live scoreboard and decides objective results when a vote cannot resolve. Never sees Secret Objectives in advance.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Player</strong></td><td>Joins by room code and is assigned a character. Sees only their own lines on their turn and a "waiting" status otherwise; swipes to advance. In Challenge Mode, also gets a private Secret Objective, takes part in races and votes, and scores.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Spectator</strong></td><td>A joined player with no character. Sees session status only. In Challenge Mode, sees race and vote status but does not score, vote, or race.</td></tr>
<tr><td><strong>Admin</strong> (internal)</td><td>Uses a separate, non-public authoring tool to manage the script library. Not a role inside the game.</td></tr>
</table></div>
</section>

<section id="s3">
<h2>3. Functional Requirements</h2>

<h3>3.1 Session Creation &amp; Joining</h3>
<ul>
<li>Host taps <strong>Host a Game</strong> (no login). The system generates a 4&ndash;6 character, case-insensitive room code that excludes ambiguous characters (<code>0/O</code>, <code>1/I</code>).</li>
<li>Host selects one of the 3 launch scripts (title, description, genre, cast size, and a "Challenge-ready" badge where applicable).</li>
<li>Players tap <strong>Join a Game</strong>, enter the room code and a display name.</li>
<li>Lobby: Host sees joined players and the cast list, and assigns players to characters. Unassigned players become Spectators; unassigned characters become auto-read (Host reads them).</li>
<li><strong>Mode toggle</strong> (Story / Challenge), default Story, locked after start. Challenge Mode is selectable only for Challenge-ready scripts and needs at least 2 players with assigned characters.</li>
<li>Host taps <strong>Start Game</strong>; the game never auto-starts.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.2 Reconnection / Session Persistence</h3>
<ul>
<li>On join, the client stores a session token in <code>localStorage</code>. Reopening the room on the same device resumes the prior seat: same character, story position, score, and objective.</li>
<li>A device with no token joins as a new player under the normal cast/spectator rules.</li>
<li>Room codes and tokens expire when the session ends or after 4 hours of inactivity.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.3 Turn-by-Turn Script Playback</h3>
<p>Scripts are a strictly linear, ordered sequence of beats (no branching in v1). Beat types:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Character line</strong>: assigned to a human player.</li>
<li><strong>Auto-read line</strong>: unassigned character; Host-controlled.</li>
<li><strong>Stage direction</strong>: descriptive text, styled differently from dialogue.</li>
<li><strong>Surprise intruder line</strong>: auto-read case for an unplanned character, usually with a sound cue.</li>
<li><strong>Objective reveal</strong> (<code>objective_reveal</code>): privately shows a Secret Objective to its owner.</li>
<li><strong>Objective check</strong> (<code>objective_check</code>): opens a group vote on whether objectives were completed.</li>
<li><strong>Reaction race</strong> (<code>reaction_race</code>): timed tap competition.</li>
<li><strong>Scoreboard</strong> (<code>scoreboard</code>): briefly shows standings.</li>
</ul>
<p>The four challenge types default to <code>challenge_only</code> and are skipped silently in Story Mode. Delays and sound cues work on every beat type.</p>
<p><strong>Visibility:</strong> only the speaking player sees the line text. Everyone else sees "[Character] is speaking&hellip;". The Host additionally sees auto-read and intruder lines, but not other humans' lines early.</p>
<p><strong>Advancing:</strong> players swipe left to deliver a line; the Host taps <strong>Next</strong> for auto-read and intruder lines. Challenge beats advance when their mechanic completes, then on the Host's Next tap where stated in 3.8&ndash;3.10.</p>
<p><strong>Line disappearance:</strong> once advanced, content is gone, with no scrollback or transcript. The one exception is a player's own Secret Objective, available through "My Objective" until resolved.</p>
<p><strong>Time delay:</strong> each beat may have an authored delay (seconds) before it becomes active.</p>

<h3>3.4 Sound System</h3>
<ul>
<li>Cues are embedded in beats and authored in advance; the Host does not trigger them.</li>
<li>Each cue has a <strong>target</strong> (a character, resolved to that player's device or the Host if unassigned, or "all devices"), a sound file, a volume (0&ndash;100%), and a loop flag.</li>
<li>Cues fire when their beat becomes active, synchronized server-side. A <code>stop_loop</code> cue type ends earlier loops.</li>
<li>Targeted cues create a natural spatial effect in a shared room.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.5 Pause / Resume</h3>
<ul>
<li>The Host can pause at any time. Pausing freezes progression, stops all audio, and holds the current visibility state; Resume restarts audio fresh from the current beat.</li>
<li>Pausing during a Reaction Race cancels it with no points; it restarts from Ready on Resume. Pausing during an objective vote holds the vote open and stops its timer.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.6 Game End</h3>
<ul>
<li>After the final beat, all clients show <strong>The End</strong> with the script title.</li>
<li><strong>Story Mode:</strong> no stats or summary.</li>
<li><strong>Challenge Mode:</strong> a final leaderboard follows, showing rank, name, character, and total for every scored player. Ties share a rank, and a highlight line appears (e.g. "Fastest reaction: [name] 212 ms"). It is shown once and not stored.</li>
<li>The room code becomes invalid after the session completes. The Host can <strong>Return to Home</strong> and start a new session.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.7 Admin / Script Authoring Tool</h3>
<ul>
<li>Hosted at a separate, unlisted URL with no links from the public app, protected by a single shared password for v1.</li>
<li>Create, edit, and delete scripts: title, description, genre, cast list, and a "Challenge-ready" indicator when at least one objective or race exists.</li>
<li><strong>Character form:</strong> name plus an optional Secret Objective (text and points; resolution is fixed to group vote with Host fallback).</li>
<li>Build the beat sequence (add, reorder, delete) with type, character, text, delay, and optional sound cue. Race fields: min/max random delay and points for ranks 1&ndash;3. Check fields: characters and vote timeout.</li>
<li>Sound cue form: target, sound file, volume, loop. Upload and manage sound assets.</li>
<li><strong>Preview mode:</strong> step through beats, toggle Story/Challenge, and simulate a race (mock tap) and a vote (mock results).</li>
<li><strong>Save-time validation:</strong> warn if a check references a character with no objective, an objective is never revealed, or an objective is revealed but never checked.</li>
<li>Publishing makes edits available to hosts immediately.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.8 Secret Objectives (Challenge Mode)</h3>
<p>Each character may have one private performance goal that does not affect the linear story, for example "Get another character to say 'key' by asking questions" or "Make someone laugh while staying in character."</p>
<p><strong>Delivery.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>At an <code>objective_reveal</code> beat, the server sends the text only to the owning player. The Host does not see it.</li>
<li>The owner can reopen it any time via <strong>My Objective</strong>.</li>
<li>Objectives for unassigned characters are never issued.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Resolution (group vote with Host fallback).</strong> At an <code>objective_check</code> beat:</p>
<ol>
<li>All players with characters except the subject see "Did [Character] complete their objective?" (Yes / No). The objective text is revealed to everyone.</li>
<li>Voting closes when all connected eligible players have voted, or after the timeout (default 20 s, authorable).</li>
<li>A simple majority Yes awards the points. A tie, or fewer than 1 eligible vote, goes to the Host (Award / Don't Award).</li>
<li>The result shows briefly ("[Character] succeeded: +2"), then the story advances on the Host's Next tap.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Rules.</strong> Players cannot vote on their own objective. Points are authored (default 2). Disconnected players are excluded from the eligible count; a disconnected subject still receives the result on reconnect. Several objectives may be resolved in one check, one at a time. Individual votes are never revealed.</p>

<h3>3.9 Reaction Race (Challenge Mode)</h3>
<p><strong>Flow.</strong></p>
<ol>
<li><strong>Ready:</strong> participants see "Get ready&hellip;" and a large tap target; Host and spectators see "Race in progress."</li>
<li><strong>Random wait:</strong> the server picks a delay in the authored range (default 2&ndash;6 s).</li>
<li><strong>GO:</strong> every participating device flashes full-screen "TAP!" and plays the beat's sound if attached. The visual flash is the authoritative signal; audio is an enhancement only.</li>
<li><strong>Tap capture:</strong> each client reports time from rendering GO to tap; the server records its own arrival time.</li>
<li><strong>Results:</strong> the race closes when all connected participants have tapped or after 3 s. Rankings show for about 4 s.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Rules.</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>False start:</strong> tapping before GO disqualifies the player for that race ("Too early!").</li>
<li><strong>Scoring:</strong> default 1st = 3, 2nd = 2, 3rd = 1, others 0, authorable per beat. Ties split by lower validated time; exact ties both get the higher points.</li>
<li><strong>Fairness:</strong> reports faster than server round-trip allows, or under a 100 ms human floor, are invalid.</li>
<li><strong>Participants:</strong> assigned-character players connected at race start; anyone who disconnects mid-race is excluded. No tap within the window scores 0.</li>
<li>Pause or Host disconnect cancels the race and restarts it from Ready. Races never block progression.</li>
</ul>

<h3>3.10 Scoring &amp; Leaderboard (Challenge Mode)</h3>
<ul>
<li>Scores come only from races and objective checks, and are held server-side.</li>
<li>The Host sees a live scoreboard. Players see only their own score during play; rankings appear at defined moments, or at an optional <code>scoreboard</code> beat.</li>
<li>Spectators and unassigned characters never appear on the leaderboard.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="s4">
<h2>4. Non-Functional Requirements</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Platform:</strong> responsive mobile web (iOS Safari, Android Chrome). Desktop for the Host is nice-to-have.</li>
<li><strong>Connectivity:</strong> reliable wifi assumed; no offline mode beyond token reconnect.</li>
<li><strong>Scale:</strong> dozens of concurrent sessions; max 6 players per session and about 10 connections per room including spectators; 3 launch scripts.</li>
<li><strong>Latency:</strong> under about 300 ms propagation spread across clients, and much lower for Reaction Race GO signals, since it affects fairness.</li>
<li><strong>Lifetime:</strong> ephemeral; no long-term storage of gameplay data, including scores.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="s5">
<h2>5. System Architecture</h2>
<h3>5.1 Components</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Client web app</strong> (Host and Player in one SPA, e.g. React).</li>
<li><strong>Admin web app</strong>, deployed separately at an unlisted URL.</li>
<li><strong>Backend API + real-time server</strong> for rooms, script serving, and state sync.</li>
<li><strong>WebSocket transport</strong> (e.g. Socket.IO, Ably, or Pusher).</li>
<li><strong>Script/asset storage:</strong> a database for scripts, objectives, and cues, plus S3-compatible object storage for sound files.</li>
<li><strong>Session state store</strong> (e.g. Redis): the authoritative live state, including mode, scores, and the active challenge.</li>
</ol>
<h3>5.2 Gameplay Data Flow</h3>
<ol>
<li>A Host action (Start, Next, Pause) goes to the server over WebSocket.</li>
<li>The server validates it against current state.</li>
<li>The server updates state and builds a tailored visibility payload for each client.</li>
<li>It sends each client its payload and dispatches any sound cue instructions.</li>
<li>Clients render their view and play targeted sounds.</li>
<li>A player swipe goes to the server, which checks it is that player's active turn, then advances the beat.</li>
</ol>
<p><strong>Challenge Mode flows:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Objective:</strong> text goes only to the owner (at reveal and on "My Objective"), and to everyone at the check reveal.</li>
<li><strong>Race:</strong> the server owns the random delay and GO timestamp; clients receive only "Ready" and "GO".</li>
<li><strong>Vote:</strong> the server tallies and sends only the aggregate result.</li>
<li><strong>Mode skipping:</strong> in Story Mode the server skips <code>challenge_only</code> beats and advances the index normally.</li>
</ul>
<h3>5.3 Why Server-Authoritative State Matters</h3>
<p>Clients must never receive data they are not allowed to see, so hiding it in the UI is not enough. The full script is never sent to a player client; they get only their own active line, status messages for others' turns, sound cues targeted at them, and in Challenge Mode their own objective and score. The Host may receive auto-read and intruder content and the live scoreboard, but never other humans' lines or Secret Objectives ahead of time.</p>
</section>

<section id="s6">
<h2>6. Data Model (Conceptual)</h2>
<h3>Script</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>script_id</code>, <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, <code>genre_tag</code></li>
<li><code>cast_list</code>: [ <code>character_id</code>, <code>character_name</code>, <code>secret_objective</code> (nullable: <code>text</code>, <code>points</code>) ]</li>
<li><code>beats</code>: ordered list of Beat objects</li>
</ul>
<h3>Beat</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>beat_id</code>, <code>order_index</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>time_delay_seconds</code> (default 0)</li>
<li><code>type</code>: <code>character_line</code> | <code>stage_direction</code> | <code>auto_read_line</code> | <code>surprise_intruder_line</code> | <code>objective_reveal</code> | <code>objective_check</code> | <code>reaction_race</code> | <code>scoreboard</code></li>
<li><code>mode</code>: <code>all</code> | <code>challenge_only</code> (challenge types default to <code>challenge_only</code>)</li>
<li><code>character_id</code> (nullable)</li>
<li><code>sound_cue</code> (nullable): <code>target</code> (<code>character_id</code> | <code>all</code>), <code>sound_asset_id</code>, <code>volume</code> (0&ndash;100), <code>loop</code>, <code>cue_type</code> (<code>play</code> | <code>stop_loop</code>)</li>
<li><code>race_config</code> (nullable): <code>min_delay_s</code>, <code>max_delay_s</code>, <code>points: [p1, p2, p3]</code></li>
<li><code>check_config</code> (nullable): <code>character_ids[]</code>, <code>vote_timeout_s</code></li>
</ul>
<h3>Sound Asset</h3>
<ul><li><code>sound_asset_id</code>, <code>filename</code> / storage reference, <code>display_name</code>, <code>duration</code> (optional)</li></ul>
<h3>Session (live state store, not long-term DB)</h3>
<ul>
<li><code>room_code</code>, <code>script_id</code>, <code>mode</code> (<code>story</code> | <code>challenge</code>), <code>status</code> (<code>lobby</code> | <code>active</code> | <code>paused</code> | <code>ended</code>), <code>current_beat_index</code></li>
<li><code>players[]</code>: <code>player_session_token</code>, <code>display_name</code>, <code>character_id</code> (null = spectator), <code>connection_status</code>, <code>score</code>, <code>objective_status</code> (<code>none</code> | <code>hidden</code> | <code>revealed</code> | <code>succeeded</code> | <code>failed</code>)</li>
<li><code>active_challenge</code> (nullable): <code>type</code>, <code>phase</code>, <code>go_timestamp</code>, <code>votes</code>, <code>taps</code></li>
<li><code>host_session_token</code>, <code>created_at</code>, <code>last_active_at</code></li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="s7">
<h2>7. Error Handling &amp; Edge Cases</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
<tr><th>Scenario</th><th>Handling</th></tr>
<tr><td>Room code not found</td><td>Inline error: "Room not found. Check the code and try again."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Room full</td><td>Joiners enter as spectators up to the cap; beyond that, "This room is full."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Host disconnects</td><td>Auto-pause (cancelling any active race). Players see "Host disconnected, waiting to resume." Host can reconnect by token; if absent past the inactivity timeout, the session ends.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Player disconnects</td><td>Shown as disconnected to the Host. No auto-pause; the story waits at their beat until they return. No timeout-based skip in v1.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Swipe when not their turn</td><td>Server ignores it; the client does not show the swipe affordance.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Same token on two devices</td><td>Latest connection wins; the older one is told the session is open elsewhere.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Sound fails to load or play</td><td>Fail silently, log to the server. Progression never blocks on audio.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Start with zero players</td><td>Blocked: "Add at least one player before starting."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Challenge Mode with under 2 assigned players</td><td>Blocked: "Challenge Mode needs at least 2 players."</td></tr>
<tr><td>Script fails to load</td><td>"Couldn't load this script, please try another or refresh"; log server-side.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Script edited during a live session</td><td>Sessions use a snapshot taken at start, so edits never affect a game in progress.</td></tr>
<tr><td>WebSocket churn</td><td>Auto-reconnect with backoff; on reconnect the client resyncs full visibility state.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Tap outside an active race</td><td>Ignored.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Duplicate taps</td><td>Only the first valid tap counts.</td></tr>
<tr><td>All players false start</td><td>No points; the story proceeds.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fewer than 2 connected participants at race start</td><td>Race is skipped silently.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Vote has no eligible voters</td><td>Host decides via Award / Don't Award.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Reconnect during a vote or race</td><td>Resync to the current phase. Past GO counts as no-tap; an open vote can still be cast if eligible.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Subject disconnects mid-check</td><td>Check proceeds; result and points apply on reconnect.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Challenge beats in Story Mode</td><td>Skipped, with the index advancing normally.</td></tr>
</table></div>
</section>

<section id="s8">
<h2>8. Security &amp; Privacy</h2>
<ul>
<li>No accounts and no PII beyond a self-chosen display name, which is not kept after the session.</li>
<li>Room codes come from a sufficiently random space to resist enumeration. Session tokens are unguessable.</li>
<li>The admin tool is unreachable from the public app (no navigation path or shared bundle routes), password-protected, and excluded from search indexing.</li>
<li>Objective text and individual votes go only to authorised clients and are not logged beyond operational need.</li>
<li>Race results are validated server-side; client-reported times are never trusted alone.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="s9">
<h2>9. Testing Plan</h2>
<h3>9.1 Unit</h3>
<ul>
<li>Beat sequencing and delays; room code uniqueness and format; token validation and seat restoration (including score and objective).</li>
<li>Visibility payloads for each client type, including that objective text reaches only its owner until the check reveal.</li>
<li>Sound cue target resolution (character, all, unassigned to Host).</li>
<li>Race ranking (ties, false starts, no-taps, too-fast reports) and vote tally (majority, tie to Host, subject and disconnected voters excluded).</li>
<li>Story Mode skipping of <code>challenge_only</code> beats with correct index advance.</li>
</ul>
<h3>9.2 Integration</h3>
<ul>
<li>Full lifecycle in Story and Challenge Mode (reveal, scene, check, race, scoreboard, leaderboard).</li>
<li>Pause/resume preserves beat, assignments, and scores; pausing during a race cancels it.</li>
<li>Host and player disconnect/reconnect at every phase, including Ready, after GO, and mid-vote.</li>
<li>Spectator overflow and auto-read/intruder flows.</li>
</ul>
<h3>9.3 Real-Time / Concurrency</h3>
<ul>
<li>Dozens of concurrent sessions with no cross-session leakage.</li>
<li>Cue and GO delivery spread across 6 clients on real wifi; per-client latency simulation to confirm the fairness check does not favour the fastest connection.</li>
<li>Race conditions: simultaneous swipes and host actions, rapid pause/resume.</li>
</ul>
<h3>9.4 Manual Playtesting</h3>
<ul>
<li>Full in-room run with 6 real devices per launch script, in both modes, checking targeted vs. broadcast audio, perceived sync, and UI readability.</li>
<li>Challenge questions: is the GO flash visible in a dim room at low brightness, are objectives achievable but non-trivial, does the group vote honestly, and is race fairness perceived across phone models.</li>
<li>Edge cases: backgrounded browser, rotated or locked phone, screen timeout, low battery.</li>
</ul>
<h3>9.5 Admin Tool</h3>
<ul>
<li>CRUD for scripts, beats, cues, and objectives, including reordering.</li>
<li>Audio upload validation (type, size); preview accuracy including Story/Challenge toggle; save-time validation warnings; snapshot isolation of live sessions.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section id="s10">
<h2>10. Out of Scope for v1</h2>
<ul>
<li>User accounts or login for hosts or players.</li>
<li>Branching or non-linear story logic.</li>
<li>Player-authored scripts or objectives.</li>
<li>Persistent stats, cross-session leaderboards, or accounts tied to scores.</li>
